>> title: Creamed Chipped Beef
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: beef, milk, breakfast, gravy, stovetop
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: chipped beef on toast, cream chipped beef, chipped beef gravy, creamed dried beef, frizzled beef, S.O.S., SOS, shit on a shingle
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min

>> step: brown 3 min, until the edges curl
Frizzle @dried beef{4%oz}(115 g; rinsed in hot water, blotted, torn in postage stamps) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) in a #saucepan{} over medium heat ~fry{3%min}, until the edges curl and go a shade darker.

>> step: cook the roux 2 min, no colour
Cook @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(30 g) into @&(~1)frizzled beef{} ~fry{2%min}, keeping it pale.

>> step: whisk in a splash at a time, simmer 6 min
Whisk @whole milk{2 1/2%cup}(600 mL) into @&(~1)beef roux{} a splash at a time, letting each one go smooth before the next, and ~simmer{6%min} until it coats a spoon.

>> step: season off the heat
Season @&(~1)creamed beef{} off the heat with @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}(2 g), @grated nutmeg{1/8%tsp} and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}(5 mL).
